s/06/06082039b7be1d9eda1c66bbec7a6c3b8a6ad9eca4686365c1538174d8ec2459.png)\n\nIntuitively, a function is a bijection if\n\n- the outputs of the function cover the entire range, and\n- every output comes from a unique input (no two inputs map to the same output).\n\n**Note:** A bijection is sometimes called a **one-to-one correspondence** because every element of the domain corresponds to exactly one element of the range, and vice versa." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186153358 #edb/ref 1065 4005 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186153358 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "69907a1e-41e6-5fdb-b8c4-325f081b7406" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186153358 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186410903 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186410939 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186410903 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186410940 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186410903 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186410941 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186410903 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186410942 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186410903 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186410943 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186410903 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045464 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186410903 #edb/ref 1045 "Bijections" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186410903 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186410939 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186410903 #edb/ref 1048 #edb/ref 17592186046673 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186410903 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186048139 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186410903 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "a9fba945-4d08-5ecb-aefa-aa4571dbef95" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186410904 #edb/ref 1080 "II only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186410904 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186410904 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "079dade0-aaba-549e-b166-40f1cd38be43" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186410905 #edb/ref 1080 "I and III only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186410905 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186410905 #edb/ref 1083